From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 10:21:50 -0700
Subject: Add GPU driver workaround
 reattach_texture_to_fbo_after_layer_increase

On PowerVR Android GPUs, when TexImage3D is called on a layered texture
(GL_TEXTURE_2D_ARRAY) whose layer count increases, if any layer of the
texture is attached to a framebuffer, the driver leaves the framebuffer
attached to old freed memory.

This adds the workaround reattach_texture_to_fbo_after_layer_increase to
the validating command buffer:
- Extends GetBindingFramebuffersForTexture to optionally include color
  attachments in addition to depth and stencil attachments.
- Updates ScopedDepthStencilReattacher in gles2_cmd_decoder.cc to detach
  all bound FBO attachments of a GL_TEXTURE_2D_ARRAY texture before
  storage reallocation when this workaround is enabled, and reattach
  immediately afterwards using glFramebufferTextureLayer.
- Adds entry 487 to gpu_driver_bug_list.json for Imagination GPUs on
  Android.

